\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Product direction (what we've worked out)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 The market:
\f1\b0  Rodeo producers (event organizers) on the desktop side, ropers (competitors) on the mobile side. Niche vertical SaaS \'97 not a unicorn, but realistic to hit $60K\'96$240K ARR with 50\'96200 producer customers at $1.2K/year. Toni and her circuit are my unfair distribution advantage; this market doesn't respond to Google Ads, it responds to word-of-mouth at events.\

\f0\b Platform decisions:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Producer tool: cross-platform desktop / web
\f1\b0  \'97 NOT Mac-only. Toni is on Windows, the rodeo demographic is on Windows. SwiftUI/macOS would be building for the wrong audience.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Roper app: iOS
\f1\b0  \'97 phones are right for glance-and-tap usage. SwiftUI work I've been doing isn't wasted, just sequenced later.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Build sequence we agreed on:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Now:
\f1\b0  Keep iterating Excel through Toni's next 1-2 rodeos. (Note: I told Claude "I can't sell option 4" \'97 meaning I won't pitch Toni on Excel-forever \'97 but Excel is fine for the immediate term while I plan/build.)\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Next:
\f1\b0  Local web app (HTML/CSS/JS) that replicates the Excel functionality. Runs from a folder on her laptop, no install, no server, no accounts. Data saves locally (browser localStorage or downloaded .json). My C# background should make JS approachable.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Then:
\f1\b0  Host the static frontend on Vercel/Netlify (free) when a second producer wants it. Each producer's data still local in their browser.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Then:
\f1\b0  Add Supabase for auth + multi-device data when a producer asks for it. First real backend.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Then:
\f1\b0  iOS roper app, sharing the same Supabase backend.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 I asked about Electron, .NET MAUI/WPF; Claude steered me toward the local web app for option 1 because it (a) cross-platform free, (b) uses skills I can ramp into quickly, (c) becomes the eventual hosted version with no rewrite.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Revenue model (for later, not now):
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Producer side: per-event pricing ($25\'9650/event) and/or monthly subscription ($30\'96100/mo). Free tier with 1 event/year as the funnel.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Roper side (later): entry fee processing \'97 take 1\'963% on top of Stripe fees on entry fees flowing through the platform. This scales with dollar volume, not user count, and is the lucrative long-term play. Optional roper subscription for stats/standings.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Adjacent later: sponsorship/ads (local feed stores, tack shops), payouts/banking partnerships, marketplace.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 First dollar realistically lands ~6\'969 months from today if I ship the local web app this month and onboard a paying producer by fall.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

